ARINC Data Loader @ADL_RELEASE_VERSION@
=====================================

What is here
------------

  adl_app           the data loader: reads a media set, finds a target and loads it
                    over ARINC 615A (or downloads from it)
  adl_media_gen     the media set generator: builds an ARINC 665 media set from files
  adl_mock_target   a mock ARINC 615A target, to try the loader against
  adl_write_payloads  writes sample media sets to a directory (command line)

  LICENSE.txt       the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later, which covers
                    these programs
  NOTICES.txt       the third-party components in this package (Qt under the LGPL,
                    the Archivo typeface under the SIL Open Font License, ...), their
                    licence texts and the offer of their source. It is also in each
                    program under About > Licences.

The Qt libraries sit beside the programs as separate files, so they can be replaced by
another build of the same Qt version, as the LGPL asks.

These programs have not been run against real aircraft equipment. The packages are not
signed for any operating system's store: your system may warn the first time you start them.

Checking the download
---------------------

Every file in a release is listed in SHA512SUMS, which is signed with the project's release
key (a detached PGP signature), and carries a build-provenance attestation that ties it
to the workflow run that built it. The steps are in
docs/verifying-releases.md in the source, and at

  @ADL_HOMEPAGE_URL@/blob/main/docs/verifying-releases.md

